Subject: Tracker holder stage: measured cap, per-row park, and stage markers

Live measurement 2026-09-21 04:12Z, `push_watch_pass.note`:
  ok:10/0 rows 10/23 pairs 10/10 miss 0 lost 0 allow 5000
  spend[setup 327/3 heal 109/1 miss0 enrolled0 pairs 204/0 rows 1320/10
        holders 1600/0] trips 14

The rotation is back (10 rows/pass over 23 active rows = ~3 passes ≈ 3 min),
and the stage split now names what is left: `holders 1600/0` — four probes
(4 × the old 400ms cap) burning ~45% of the pass and writing NOTHING, while
every `holders_checked_at` row in `push_watch` sat 15-20h stale. The endpoint
itself was healthy (`/debug/birdeye-overview` on live tracked mints: 303 /
305 / 673 / 816 / 907 / 2_870 ms), so 400ms sat below its own common latency,
and because a miss writes nothing the due list (oldest-check first) re-offered
the same slow head on every pass.

Fix, three parts:
  - cap 400 → 1_200ms (covers the measured common range);
  - a MISS now parks that row for TRACKER_HOLDER_BACKOFF_MS (10 min, under the
    30-min refresh interval), so a slow row cannot hold the stage's slots
    while the rows behind it never get a turn;
  - the stage reports `held N cut M` next to its clock, so a starved holder
    stage is visible in /health instead of hiding behind `holders 1600/0`.

